## Orchestration (global repo)

This repository is the **orchestration repo**: it owns global requirements and
dispatches work to service repos. It contains no service code.

1. `docs/services.md` is the hand-maintained service registry (dev repos + manual
   platforms). `docs/service-dependencies.md` is a derived view — regenerate it from
   the registry and each dev repo's AGENTS.md / architecture.md before planning; never
   hand-edit it.
2. Run `devsop-plan` / `devsop-design` here on business-level stories. Do not split
   stories by service; service impact is decided by design's architecture recon.
3. Dispatch by `tasks.md` Component: each service repo receives a projection at
   `docs/plans/<dir-id>/` (its tasks + relevant criteria/test cases + interface
   contract summary) with a back-link to this repo and commit hash. Projections are
   generated, never hand-edited.
4. Cross-service integration verification and deployment ordering run here, against
   the original acceptance criteria in this repo.
5. Service-internal docs (coding style, tests, API standards) live in the service
   repos — link them, do not copy them here.
